research/audit/wave7-refuter-tasks/cor-perfect-normality-is-hereditary.md-59-1.2 Let $F$ be closed in $S$. Write $F=C\cap S$ with $C$ closed in $X$; perfect normality writes $C=\bigcap_{n\in\mathbb N}U_n$ with every $U_n$ open in $X$. [F1]
research/audit/wave7-refuter-tasks/cor-perfect-normality-is-hereditary.md-60-
research/audit/wave7-refuter-tasks/cor-perfect-normality-is-hereditary.md-61-2.1 Then $F=\bigcap_{n\in\mathbb N}(U_n\cap S)$, a $G_\delta$ of $S$. Thus $S$ is perfectly normal, and with its inherited $T_1$ property it is $T_6$ when $X$ is $T_6$. [F1, step 1.1, step 1.2] ∎
